{"chunk_id": "da4f2ef64bd8", "text": "After cursing the sons of Vasistha, the formidable sage Vishwamitra turns his attention to King Trishanku, who seeks the impossible: to enter heaven in his physical body. The gathered sages, fearing Vishwamitra\u2019s legendary temper and the power of his asceticism, reluctantly assist him in a grand sacrifice. Yet when the rites are completed and the gods are invoked, none appear. Enraged, Vishwamitra uses his spiritual power to propel Trishanku bodily into the heavens. Indra rejects the king\u2014already cursed by his guru\u2014and hurls him back toward earth. As Trishanku falls, he cries out for help, and Vishwamitra halts him mid\u2011descent, suspending him in the sky. In fury, the sage begins creating an entirely new cosmos\u2014stars, planets, and even rival gods\u2014until the frightened deities negotiate a compromise: Trishanku will remain eternally suspended in a heaven fashioned by Vishwamitra. The episode reveals the terrifying creative power of ascetic austerity and the tension between sages and gods.\nVishwamitra forces a sacrifice for Trishanku, sends him bodily to heaven, and when the gods reject him, creates a new heaven where Trishanku hangs suspended.\nThemes: ascetic power, defiance of gods, curse and cosmic order, creation of new heaven, guru conflict", "vector": [0.010855942964553833, -0.01796606555581093, 0.010876752436161041, 0.0009451259975321591, -0.00835872907191515, 0.034378308802843094, -0.028412742540240288, -0.02927289344370365, -0.00372847868129611, -0.026498211547732353, 0.014123130589723587, 0.015732446685433388, 0.02348768152296543, 0.004522731527686119, 0.003756225574761629, -0.007956400513648987, 0.04778002202510834, -0.013505764305591583, 0.007505514193326235, -0.008552956394851208, -0.005264958832412958, -0.012326523661613464, -0.004349313676357269, 0.026151375845074654, -0.024930516257882118, 0.015621459111571312, 0.021365050226449966, -0.021226316690444946, -0.0010864613577723503, -0.0226